# Typography – hyphen, not em dash

- In **English (and French) UI strings**, **meta text**, **portfolio copy**, **alt text**, **comments meant for maintainers when they quote UI**, and similar: use the **ASCII hyphen-minus** `-` instead of the **em dash** `—` (U+2014).
- Prefer **spaced pairs** for readability where an em dash would have been used as a pause or separator: ` - ` (e.g. `Role - Lead`, `2024 - Present`).
- **Do not** introduce em dashes in new copy; if you edit a line that still contains `—`, normalize it to `-` / ` - ` as appropriate.
